      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0153",
    "text": "How old is Earth?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2434,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "moving-earth-geology-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0154",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. Radioactive decay gives a way to measure ages in years. Compare mineral clocks with the meteorite evidence used to estimate Earth's formation age.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2435,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "moving-earth-geology-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2436,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "moving-earth-geology-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0155",
    "text": "What happens to life when land moves?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2437,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "moving-earth-geology-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0156",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. Ocean-floor patterns support moving plates and the recycling of crust. Reconsider the distribution of living things on this changing surface.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2438,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "moving-earth-geology-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2439,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "moving-earth-geology-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0157",
    "text": "What can explicit rules make a machine do?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2440,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "computing",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0158",
    "text": "This comparison covers c. 1847\u20131950. Logical relationships can be represented by symbols, switches and explicit instructions. Compare an abstract procedure with a machine that carries it out.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2441,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "computing",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2442,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "computing",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0159",
    "text": "Can a program always tell whether another will stop?\nHow can a machine correct its actions?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2443,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "computing-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0160",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. A general-purpose machine faces a demand no procedure can always satisfy. Then compare computation with a feedback loop that adjusts action toward a target.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2444,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "computing-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2445,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "computing-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0161",
    "text": "Can a damaged message be recovered?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2446,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "computing-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0162",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. Investigate how noise can damage a transmitted message. Structured extra information can correct specified errors without proving the message true.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2447,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "computing-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2448,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "computing-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0163",
    "text": "Can the same words become a different work?\nDoes a scholarly-looking source have to be real?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2449,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "borges",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0164",
    "text": "These records cover c. 1930\u20131960. In Borges's fictional example, the same words are written in a different historical setting. Compare their changed interpretation with a literary archive that invents its sources.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2450,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "borges",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2451,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "borges",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0165",
    "text": "Can a map contain too much detail?\nMust a story choose one path?\nWho gains power when art is copied?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2452,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "borges-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0166",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. Compare an unusably complete map, a branching story and copied artwork. Each asks what a representation selects or changes rather than merely duplicates.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2453,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "borges-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2454,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "borges-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0167",
    "text": "How did these values gain authority?\nWho is left out of a universal claim?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2455,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "categories",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0168",
    "text": "This comparison covers c. 1887\u20131990. These accounts examine how moral values and supposedly universal classifications gain authority. Look at particular histories and exclusions rather than rejecting every claim at once.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2456,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "categories",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2457,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "categories",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0169",
    "text": "What gives a category its meaning?\nHow do classifications shape people's lives?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2458,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "categories-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0170",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. Compare categories defined by relationships with classifications used in institutions. Consider how those practices shape conduct.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2459,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "categories-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2460,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "categories-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0171",
    "text": "Does this argument contradict its own example?\nCan limited viewpoints still be checked?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2461,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "categories-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0172",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. Examine a critic's conflicting claims about originals and copies. Then compare the limits of an observer's viewpoint with the possibility of independent checks.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2462,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "categories-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2463,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "categories-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0173",
    "text": "Do genes determine a whole life?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2464,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0174",
    "text": "This comparison covers c. 1900\u20132020. Distinct inherited factors and DNA address the earlier problem of heredity. Development and environment still matter; genes are not a complete prediction of an organism's life.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2465,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2466,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0175",
    "text": "How does industry change the climate?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2467,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0176",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. Connect fossil-fuel emissions with the way greenhouse gases affect heat loss. Compare that explanation with records of global warming.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2468,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2469,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0177",
    "text": "What can old air tell us?\nWhere did the extra lead come from?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2470,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0178",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. Old air bubbles preserve atmospheric history. Lead contamination in dating work also becomes evidence about modern pollution; these records answer different questions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2471,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2472,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0179",
    "text": "Does geography decide history?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2473,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "planet-session-4",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0180",
    "text": "Later that day, the worktable is ready for another session. Connect organisms through food webs and revisit the history of forced labour in trade. Geography and ecology affect human choices without determining them.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2474,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "planet-session-4",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2475,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "planet-session-4",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0181",
    "text": "What if the model meets an unfamiliar case?\nWhat would make this finding more convincing?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2476,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0182",
    "text": "Imagine a remote observatory. Compare a model's predictions with a proposed trial, an unfamiliar case and readings from separate instruments.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2477,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2479,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0183",
    "text": "Imagine an observatory far from Earth. It needs ways to check its findings and decide what it may do before a reply arrives.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2478,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "skip bridge",
        "owner": "future-laboratory",
        "field": "onAlreadyComplete.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0184",
    "text": "Can others check the distant finding?\nWhen should the local system stop and ask?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2480,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-laboratory-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0185",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. The remote observatory needs authority limits while Earth is out of contact. Keep records of how findings were made and protect their transmission, while keeping their limits visible.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2481,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-laboratory-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2482,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-laboratory-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0186",
    "text": "Who will do the necessary care?\nMust everyone want the same good life?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2483,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0187",
    "text": "These imagined workshops apply earlier arguments about useful work and control. Machinery can save effort while care and other demanding work still need to be shared.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2484,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2486,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0188",
    "text": "People can challenge and revise the community's shared rules. They still need to organize care, divide work fairly and make room for different ways of living.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2485,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "completion/ending",
        "owner": "future-commons",
        "field": "completionText"
      },
      {
        "row": 2492,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "completion/ending",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "completionText"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0189",
    "text": "Who can challenge a rapid decision?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2487,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-2",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0190",
    "text": "It is evening. The worktable is cleared for a new session. A city's quick response meets residents' conflicting priorities. Provide a way to inspect and challenge decisions while acknowledging the cost of delay.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2488,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-2",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2489,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-2",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0191",
    "text": "How can we keep shared rules open to change?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2490,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "objective",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "objectives"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0192",
    "text": "The next morning, we return to a cleared worktable. How can people affected by shared resources challenge and revise the rules? Care, fair work and disagreement still need attention.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2491,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "entry fallback",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "motivation"
      },
      {
        "row": 2493,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "story body",
        "owner": "future-commons-session-3",
        "field": "entryCue.text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0731",
    "text": "Divinity: Disputed Questions",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4314,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "chooser",
        "owner": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "field": "title"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0732",
    "text": "A manuscript desk, not a test of faith. Follow a wound, a failed promise, bread, a hungry household and a request for prayer through changing arguments. Build what each writer is claiming, test it against a case, and leave real disagreements open. New chapters reuse distinctions you have made; Read offers short explanations, not a hidden recipe book.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4315,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "chooser",
        "owner": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "field": "premise"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0733",
    "text": "Case: a cut body has lost its health",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4316,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "cut-body",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0734",
    "text": "Imagine an injured person. The body remains, but it is not as sound as it should be. Nothing here says that the injured person deserves the injury.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4317,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "cut-body",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0735",
    "text": "Case: the wound heals; no evil thing escapes",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4318,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "healed-body",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0736",
    "text": "The injury disappears as the body heals. This is Augustine\u2019s kind of example: the loss is repaired, rather than a second material being removed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4319,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "healed-body",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0737",
    "text": "Case: I take the meal my neighbour needs",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4320,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "stolen-meal",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0738",
    "text": "Imagine taking another person\u2019s share for your own comfort, knowing whose share it is. This is a deliberate action, unlike merely suffering a wound.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4321,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "stolen-meal",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0739",
    "text": "Comfort is good; my neighbour is still owed food",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4322,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "fair-share",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0740",
    "text": "Enjoying food is good, but the neighbour is still owed their share. The wrong is taking that food, not enjoying a meal.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4323,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "fair-share",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0741",
    "text": "Genesis: creation was \u201cvery good\u201d",
    "occurrences": [
      {
