        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "maker-knows",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0789",
    "text": "An observer can foresee harm without making its cause",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4378,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "watcher-only",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0790",
    "text": "Foreknowledge alone need not cause an event. This is the kind of reply examined in the text. A creator\u2019s additional role still needs attention.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4379,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "watcher-only",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0791",
    "text": "The writer turns the tree saying into a rule about causes",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4380,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "good-source-limit",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0792",
    "text": "The writer reads the tree-and-fruit saying as a rule about the sources of good and evil. Accepting the verse does not require accepting that particular interpretation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4381,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "good-source-limit",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0793",
    "text": "Two Principles: good and evil must have opposed sources",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4382,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-sources",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0794",
    "text": "The writer of the Book of Two Principles sees both good and harm in the world. Because the writer holds that a wholly good source cannot cause evil, the argument requires opposed sources. This conflicts with Augustine's account of evil as damaged goodness.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4383,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "two-sources",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0795",
    "text": "A knowing maker is not merely a knowing spectator",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4384,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "maker-not-watcher",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4756,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-maker-not-watcher",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0796",
    "text": "Knowing that harm will happen is different from making the conditions that cause it. A reply about a passive observer does not fully answer the question about a knowing creator.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4385,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "maker-not-watcher",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4755,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-maker-not-watcher",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0797",
    "text": "Is evil damaged goodness, or does it have its own source?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4386,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "origins-dispute",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4758,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-origins-dispute",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0798",
    "text": "Augustine says evil is damage within a good creation. The writer of the Book of Two Principles argues that a wholly good source cannot cause evil, so evil must have an opposed source. The two accounts give different answers to the same problem of suffering and wrongdoing.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4387,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "origins-dispute",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4757,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-origins-dispute",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0799",
    "text": "Aquinas: fire does what fire does\u2014it heats and burns",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4388,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "fire-active",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0800",
    "text": "For Aquinas, fire functions well as fire when it heats and burns. That does not make it morally good or mean that every effect is good for everything nearby.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4389,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "fire-active",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0801",
    "text": "Aquinas\u2019s example: the fire works, but destroys the water",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4390,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "water-lost",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0802",
    "text": "Aquinas imagines fire working according to its nature while destroying water. His medieval account concerns the loss of what makes it water, not a modern chemistry explanation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4391,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "water-lost",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0803",
    "text": "Aquinas: the world can give reasons to believe in its cause",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4392,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "reason-effects",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0804",
    "text": "Aquinas thinks reasoning from effects can establish some things about their cause. \u201cCreatures\u201d in his text means created things, not only animals. He does not think such reasoning establishes every Christian belief.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4393,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "reason-effects",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0805",
    "text": "Aquinas: the world cannot prove Father, Son and Spirit are one God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4394,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "faith-beyond",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0806",
    "text": "The Trinity is the belief that Father, Son and Holy Spirit are one God, not three gods. Aquinas says observation of created things cannot prove this belief.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4395,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "faith-beyond",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0807",
    "text": "Fire can work well as fire while harming something else",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4396,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "good-can-harm",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0808",
    "text": "Fire can function well as fire while harming something else. This challenges a rule that treats good functioning and harmless effects as the same thing.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4397,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "good-can-harm",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0809",
    "text": "Aquinas: harmful effects do not require a separate evil source",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4398,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-not-forced",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0810",
    "text": "Aquinas's example offers a way for harmful effects to come from something functioning well. It challenges the need for a separate evil source without answering every question about suffering.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4399,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "two-not-forced",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0811",
    "text": "Explaining a belief is not the same as proving it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4400,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "reason-boundary",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4762,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-reason-boundary",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0812",
    "text": "Aquinas distinguishes explaining a belief from proving it. He allows reasoning about the Trinity while denying that observations of created things can establish it.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4401,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "reason-boundary",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0813",
    "text": "The fire example challenges two sources, but leaves the maker\u2019s responsibility open",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4402,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "limited-answer",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4760,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-limited-answer",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0814",
    "text": "The fire example challenges the claim that every harmful effect needs a wholly evil source. It still leaves the question of why a knowing creator would make a world in which such harm occurs.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4403,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "limited-answer",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0815",
    "text": "Teacher and pupil have different roles; both are human",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4404,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "teacher-pupil",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0816",
    "text": "A teacher and pupil have different roles while both remaining human. A difference in relationship does not automatically mean a difference in the kind of being they are.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4405,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "teacher-pupil",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0817",
    "text": "Augustine: Father and Son name a relationship, not two kinds of God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4406,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "father-word",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0818",
    "text": "Father and Son name a relationship, not two kinds of God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4407,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "father-word",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4408,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "father-word",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0819",
    "text": "Being someone's father describes a relationship; it does not make the father a different kind of being from the child. Augustine uses this distinction to explain the names Father and Son while holding that both are divine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4409,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "father-word",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0820",
    "text": "Does being Son mean being a lesser kind of God?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4410,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "less-divine-question",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0821",
    "text": "This is a question about an inference from the titles. Being related differently does not, just by itself, decide whether two are unequal in nature.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4411,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "less-divine-question",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0822",
    "text": "Case: three humans share a kind, but remain three beings",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4412,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "three-humans",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0823",
    "text": "Calling three people \u201chuman\u201d does not turn them into a single human being. This comparison exposes a tempting but misleading way to explain divine unity.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4413,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "three-humans",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0824",
    "text": "Augustine: Father, Son and Spirit are one divine being",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4414,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "one-divine-being",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0825",
    "text": "Father, Son and Spirit are one divine being",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4415,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "one-divine-being",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4416,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "one-divine-being",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0826",
    "text": "Augustine says Father, Son and Holy Spirit are one divine being. He also distinguishes them: the names do not all refer to the same relationship.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4417,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "one-divine-being",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0827",
    "text": "Jesus: \u201cFather \u2026 glorify thy Son\u201d",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4418,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "son-addresses",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0828",
    "text": "The Son addresses the Father. Augustine must explain how this real relationship belongs within his belief in one God.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4419,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "son-addresses",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0829",
    "text": "Different relationships need not mean different kinds of being",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4420,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "relation-not-kind",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0830",
    "text": "Teacher and pupil have different roles while both being human. Augustine similarly treats Father and Son as names of a relationship, not names for greater and lesser kinds of God.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4421,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "relation-not-kind",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0831",
    "text": "Augustine: the name Son does not mean a lesser God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4422,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-less-divine",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4764,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-not-less-divine",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0832",
    "text": "the name Son does not mean a lesser God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4423,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-less-divine",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4424,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-less-divine",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      },
      {
        "row": 4765,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder owned-location italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-not-less-divine",
        "field": "item.labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4766,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder owned-location italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-not-less-divine",
        "field": "item.labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0833",
    "text": "Augustine says Son names a relationship to the Father, not an inferior kind of God. On his account, Father and Son share the same divine nature.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4425,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "not-less-divine",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4763,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-not-less-divine",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0834",
    "text": "Augustine: one God\u2014not three gods sharing a kind",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4426,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-three-members",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0835",
    "text": "one God\u2014not three gods sharing a kind",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4427,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-three-members",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4428,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-three-members",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0836",
    "text": "Three humans share a kind but remain three separate beings. Augustine's claim is different: Father, Son and Spirit are one divine being with real distinctions, not three similar gods.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4429,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "not-three-members",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0837",
    "text": "Augustine: Father and Son are distinct, not one actor changing masks",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4430,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-masks",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0838",
    "text": "Father and Son are distinct, not one actor changing masks",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4431,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-masks",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4432,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-masks",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0839",
    "text": "In Augustine's account, Father and Son are genuinely distinct: the Son addresses the Father. They are not one actor successively wearing different costumes.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4433,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "not-masks",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0840",
    "text": "Trinity: one God as Father, Son and Holy Spirit",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4434,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trinity-bounded",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4768,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-trinity-bounded",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0841",
    "text": "The doctrine of the Trinity names Father, Son and Holy Spirit as one God. They are not separate gods or one person taking turns in different roles. Aquinas says observation of created things cannot prove this doctrine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4435,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trinity-bounded",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4767,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-trinity-bounded",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0842",
    "text": "Lyon ritual: a Gospel book and hands touch the candidate",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4436,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "book-and-hands",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0843",
    "text": "A Gospel is an account of Jesus\u2019s life and teaching. The ritual places the book and hands on the candidate. These are physical actions, even though the ceremony claims an inward gift.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4437,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "book-and-hands",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0844",
    "text": "Lyon ritual: laying on hands gives forgiveness and God\u2019s Spirit",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4438,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "spirit-baptism",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0845",
    "text": "The Lyon rite promises forgiveness and the Holy Spirit, understood as God dwelling with the believer. It calls the laying on of hands spiritual baptism rather than washing with water.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4439,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "spirit-baptism",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0846",
    "text": "Acts: Jesus\u2019s first followers lay on hands to give the Spirit",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4440,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "acts-hands-line",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0847",
    "text": "Acts is the biblical account of the early Christian community. The ritual cites its report that Peter and John lay hands on believers who receive the Holy Spirit. The appeal claims authority; it is not independent verification of this later rite.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4441,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "acts-hands-line",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0848",
    "text": "Lyon candidate promises to turn from worldly desires",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4442,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "world-renunciation",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0849",
    "text": "The candidate promises to turn away from \u201cworldly desires\u201d. This concerns how the person should live; it does not state a complete explanation of who created matter.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4443,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "world-renunciation",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0850",
    "text": "Jesus: \u201cLove your enemies\u201d",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4444,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "enemy-love",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0851",
    "text": "Loving enemies is one of the candidate's obligations. Turning away from worldly desires therefore cannot mean abandoning concern for other people.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4445,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "enemy-love",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0852",
    "text": "Lyon ritual claims to continue the first followers\u2019 laying on of hands",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4446,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "apostolic-claim",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0853",
    "text": "The Lyon ritual appeals to the laying on of hands described among Jesus's first followers. Its ministers claim authority by continuing that practice.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4447,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "apostolic-claim",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0854",
    "text": "The rite claims a spiritual gift through hands and a book",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4448,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "bodily-spiritual",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0855",
    "text": "The ritual uses a person's body, ministers' hands and a Gospel book while claiming a spiritual gift. Physical action and a claimed inward effect are not simple opposites.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4449,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "bodily-spiritual",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0856",
    "text": "Using bodies in a rite does not prove belief in one good creator",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4450,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "ritual-not-cosmology",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4770,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-ritual-not-cosmology",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0857",
    "text": "Hands and a book show that the rite uses physical objects. They do not establish whether its community believed in one good creator or opposed sources. The Lyon ritual and the Book of Two Principles must not be merged into one universal Cathar doctrine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4451,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "ritual-not-cosmology",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4769,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-ritual-not-cosmology",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0858",
    "text": "Rejecting worldly desires does not cancel the duty to love enemies",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4452,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "renounce-not-abandon",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4772,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-renounce-not-abandon",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0859",
    "text": "The candidate promises to reject worldly desires and to love enemies. Giving up those desires does not remove duties toward other people.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4453,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "renounce-not-abandon",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4771,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-renounce-not-abandon",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0860",
    "text": "Aquinas\u2019s example: the axe cuts the wood",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4454,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "axe-cuts",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0861",
    "text": "The edge explains the tool\u2019s ordinary cutting. It does not explain by itself why a particular piece of furniture takes shape.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4455,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "axe-cuts",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0862",
    "text": "The craftsperson uses the axe to make a bed",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4456,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "craftsman-shapes",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0863",
    "text": "The craftsperson and the tool act in different, connected ways. Calling the axe effective does not install a second independent designer.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4457,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "craftsman-shapes",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0864",
    "text": "Baptism uses water to wash the body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4458,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "water-washes",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0865",
    "text": "Water has an ordinary bodily action. Aquinas cites Augustine\u2019s distinction between touching the body and cleansing the heart.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4459,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "water-washes",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0866",
    "text": "Aquinas: only God gives grace\u2014new life within the soul",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4460,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "god-grace",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0867",
    "text": "For Aquinas, grace is God\u2019s gift of a new share in divine life, changing the soul from within. God alone is its ultimate source.\n\nHis question is whether a bodily rite can truly help bring about that gift without becoming a second, independent source of divine power.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4461,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "god-grace",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0868",
    "text": "Aquinas: God appointed baptism with water to give grace\u2014new life within the soul",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4462,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "instituted-baptism",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0869",
    "text": "Aquinas says God chose baptism as a way to give grace: a new life within the soul. That is why its water has a role beyond ordinary washing.\n\nA sacrament is such a God-appointed bodily sign or rite. The axe comparison cannot prove that God appointed any particular rite.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4463,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "instituted-baptism",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0870",
    "text": "Aquinas: \u201cgrace does not destroy nature, but perfects it\u201d \u2014 gloss: God\u2019s help develops human powers rather than erasing them",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4464,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "nature-perfected-line",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0871",
    "text": "God's gift of help develops human powers such as reasoning and willing rather than erasing them. Aquinas describes reason serving faith and willing guided by love. This does not mean a person becomes incapable of error, and questions about free choice remain.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4465,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "nature-perfected-line",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0872",
    "text": "The axe cuts; the craftsperson works through it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4466,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "dependent-tool",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0873",
    "text": "The axe cuts the wood, while the craftsperson makes the bed through it. Both act, but the axe is not a second independent maker. Aquinas uses this pattern to explain how God could act through a rite.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4467,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "dependent-tool",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0874",
    "text": "Aquinas: a rite can be God\u2019s tool, not a second god",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4468,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "dependent-grace",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0875",
    "text": "Aquinas argues that God can act through a rite as a craftsperson acts through a tool. This explains how the rite need not rival God, but does not prove that God appointed any particular ceremony.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4469,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "dependent-grace",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0876",
    "text": "Aquinas: God chose baptism with water to give inward grace, not just wash the body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4470,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "baptism-appointed",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0877",
    "text": "Aquinas believes God chose baptism with water to give inward grace. The water acts through God's choice; it does not gain independent divine power.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4471,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "baptism-appointed",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0878",
    "text": "Aquinas: in baptism, God works through water to give inward grace",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4472,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "instrumental-baptism",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4774,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-instrumental-baptism",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0879",
    "text": "For Aquinas, baptism washes the body while God works through the rite to give inward grace. The water is God's instrument, not a second god. This depends on his further belief that God appointed baptism; ordinary water is not automatically a sacrament.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4473,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "instrumental-baptism",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4773,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-instrumental-baptism",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0880",
    "text": "God\u2019s help need not stop a person from really choosing",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4474,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "help-not-erasure",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4778,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-help-not-erasure",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0881",
    "text": "Augustine's helped person still chooses, and Aquinas's tool still acts. The comparison shows that dependent action can be real; it does not mean people are merely tools.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4475,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "help-not-erasure",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0882",
    "text": "Both rites use bodies; they disagree about what God appointed",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4476,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "rites-different",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4776,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-rites-different",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0883",
    "text": "The Lyon rite uses hands and a Gospel book; Aquinas discusses baptism with water. Both claim an inward gift through physical actions, but disagree about the authorized rite and how it gives that gift.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4477,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "rites-different",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4775,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-rites-different",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0884",
    "text": "Case: after the church\u2019s blessing, it still looks and tastes like bread",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4478,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "bread-taste",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0885",
    "text": "After the blessing, the bread looks and tastes the same. Aquinas's account must explain why he still says that what it is has changed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4479,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "bread-taste",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0886",
    "text": "Jesus: \u201cThis is my body\u201d",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4480,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "supper-words",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0887",
    "text": "Christians dispute what these supper words mean. Aquinas reads them as affirming the real presence of Christ\u2019s body, not only a reminder.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4481,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "supper-words",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0888",
    "text": "Aquinas: what was bread becomes Christ\u2019s body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4482,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "aquinas-change",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0889",
    "text": "Aquinas says the bread becomes Christ\u2019s body, although its taste, colour and shape remain. He is not saying that it starts to look or taste like flesh.\n\nThis claim is called transubstantiation: a change in what the thing is, while its appearances remain. Other Christians dispute the claim.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4483,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "aquinas-change",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0890",
    "text": "Aquinas: what a thing is can differ from how it looks and tastes",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4484,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "appearance-rule",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0891",
    "text": "Aquinas distinguishes what something is from its appearance. In Communion, he says the bread's substance\u2014what it is\u2014changes, while qualities such as taste and colour remain. He calls those remaining qualities accidents.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4485,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "appearance-rule",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0892",
    "text": "Aquinas reads Christ\u2019s words as changing bread into his body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4486,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "changed-claim",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0893",
    "text": "Aquinas reads Christ's supper words as saying that bread becomes Christ's body. This is a particular interpretation, not the only possible reading established by the words alone.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4487,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "changed-claim",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0894",
    "text": "For Aquinas, unchanged taste does not mean unchanged reality",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4488,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "same-appearances",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0895",
    "text": "Aquinas says the appearance stays the same while what the thing is changes. Unchanged taste therefore does not contradict his account, but it does not verify it either.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4489,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "same-appearances",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0896",
    "text": "Aquinas: it becomes Christ\u2019s body but keeps bread\u2019s look and taste",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4490,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "eucharist-account",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0897",
    "text": "Aquinas says the bread becomes Christ's body while keeping the look and taste of bread. This is called transubstantiation. Explaining the claim about Communion does not establish that the change occurred.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4491,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "eucharist-account",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0898",
    "text": "This explains Aquinas\u2019s claim; tasting the bread does not prove it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4492,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "not-sensory-proof",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4780,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-not-sensory-proof",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0899",
    "text": "Tasting the bread cannot prove the change Aquinas describes, because he says its taste remains. His account rests on faith in divine authority, not on a hidden change detected by the senses.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4493,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "not-sensory-proof",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4779,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-not-sensory-proof",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0900",
    "text": "Aquinas: baptism\u2019s water is God\u2019s tool; Communion\u2019s bread becomes Christ\u2019s body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4494,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-material-roles",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4782,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-two-material-roles",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0901",
    "text": "For Aquinas, baptism's water is a tool through which God acts. In Communion, what was bread becomes Christ's body while appearances remain. These give physical things different roles.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4495,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "two-material-roles",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4781,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-two-material-roles",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0902",
    "text": "Case: the household has one coin and no supper",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4496,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "single-coin",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0903",
    "text": "The household has one coin and no supper. Spending it on an indulgence would leave the family's immediate need for food unmet.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4497,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "single-coin",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0904",
    "text": "Seller\u2019s claim reported by Luther: a coin frees a dead soul",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4498,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "seller-guarantee",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0905",
    "text": "Luther reports sellers promising that payment releases a dead person from punishment. He attacks the claim that a coin can guarantee that result.\n\nThe punishment in question is purgatory: purification after death for people ultimately saved, not hell. A reported sales pitch is not the same as official doctrine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4499,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "seller-guarantee",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0906",
    "text": "An indulgence concerns penalties remaining after sins are forgiven",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4500,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "letter-penalties",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0907",
    "text": "In this debate, being forgiven can still leave penalties to be dealt with. An indulgence concerns those penalties; it is not supposed to buy forgiveness itself.\n\nLuther questions what the pope can release. The seller\u2019s promised release of a dead soul is a disputed sales claim, not an official definition of Catholic teaching.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4501,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "letter-penalties",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0908",
    "text": "Luther: household necessities and poor neighbours come first",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4502,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "care-first-rule",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0909",
    "text": "Luther gives care a positive priority, rather than treating the purchase as the only religious use for money.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4503,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "care-first-rule",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0910",
    "text": "Luther: the pope announces forgiveness; God is the one who forgives",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4504,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "declare-forgiveness",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0911",
    "text": "In 1517 Luther still allows a ministerial role. Declaring God\u2019s forgiveness is not an independent power to make God forgive on receipt of money.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4505,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "declare-forgiveness",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0912",
    "text": "Luther: repentance means a lifetime of turning away from wrong",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4506,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "repent-whole-life",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0913",
    "text": "Repentance is turning from wrong, not a transaction completed once and forgotten. This claim helps explain why a guarantee based on payment troubles Luther.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4507,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "repent-whole-life",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0914",
    "text": "For Luther, a seller cannot guarantee God\u2019s mercy for a coin",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4508,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "coin-not-control",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0915",
    "text": "Luther rejects a seller's guarantee that a payment will release a dead soul. A limited church role does not give the seller control over God's mercy.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4509,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "coin-not-control",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0916",
    "text": "Luther: buy the hungry household supper before an indulgence letter",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4510,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "feed-before-letter",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4784,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-feed-before-letter",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0917",
    "text": "Luther gives household necessities and help for poor neighbours priority over buying an indulgence. With one coin and no supper, the household should buy food first.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4511,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "feed-before-letter",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4783,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-feed-before-letter",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0918",
    "text": "Working for God does not mean controlling God\u2019s gifts",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4512,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "ministry-not-sale",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4786,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-ministry-not-sale",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0919",
    "text": "A person can serve God without controlling God's gifts. Comparing Luther's limits on church authority with Aquinas's dependent instrument clarifies that distinction without making their doctrines identical.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4513,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "ministry-not-sale",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4785,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-ministry-not-sale",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0920",
    "text": "Luther: a paid guarantee cannot replace a changed life",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4514,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "no-paid-shortcut",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4788,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-no-paid-shortcut",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0921",
    "text": "For Luther, a guarantee based on payment cannot replace repentance and a changed life. This criticism is not a blanket claim that every church rite or payment is fraudulent.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4515,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "no-paid-shortcut",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0922",
    "text": "Luther: faith (trust in Christ), not good deeds, makes us right with God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4516,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "gift-acceptance",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0923",
    "text": "Luther says faith, or trust in Christ and his promise, makes a person right with God. This is called justification. Helping a neighbour meets a real need, but does not earn God's acceptance.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4517,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "gift-acceptance",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0924",
    "text": "Case: if God accepts me without payment, why feed anyone?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4518,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "why-help",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0925",
    "text": "A reader takes Luther's rejection of earning God's acceptance as a reason to do nothing. But a neighbour still needs help. What should good deeds accomplish?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4519,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "why-help",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0926",
    "text": "Case: the neighbour\u2019s hunger has not vanished",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4520,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "neighbour-still-hungry",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0927",
    "text": "Freedom from buying God\u2019s acceptance does not itself supply the neighbour\u2019s food. The case asks who a good work is for.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4521,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "neighbour-still-hungry",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0928",
    "text": "Luther: Christ served me freely; I can freely serve my neighbour",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4522,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "christ-serves",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0929",
    "text": "Luther says Christians should serve their neighbours freely, as Christ served them. They help because the neighbour needs it, not to earn God's acceptance.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4523,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "christ-serves",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0930",
    "text": "Luther: train the body to serve, not to earn God\u2019s acceptance",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4524,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "body-practice",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0931",
    "text": "The text does not discard bodily life. Work and discipline remain, but their role must be distinguished from earning acceptance.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4525,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "body-practice",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0932",
    "text": "Not earning God\u2019s acceptance does not make helping others pointless",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4526,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "no-wages",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0933",
    "text": "Feeding someone can help them even if it does not earn acceptance by God. Luther gives service a purpose in the neighbour's need rather than treating it as a payment for salvation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4527,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "no-wages",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0934",
    "text": "Luther: feed the neighbour because they need food, not to earn salvation",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4528,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "free-service",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0935",
    "text": "Luther calls for service because the neighbour needs help, following Christ's freely given service. The deed is not a price paid to earn God's acceptance.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4529,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "free-service",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0936",
    "text": "Feeding the household helps people; it does not buy acceptance by God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4530,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "care-not-purchase",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4790,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-care-not-purchase",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0937",
    "text": "The household still needs supper. For Luther, feeding them serves that need without buying acceptance by God. A good deed can matter to other people without becoming payment for salvation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4531,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "care-not-purchase",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4789,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-care-not-purchase",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0938",
    "text": "Augustine: what helps me act? Luther: what makes me right with God?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4532,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-grace-questions",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4792,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-two-grace-questions",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0939",
    "text": "what helps me act? Luther: what makes me right with God?",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4533,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-grace-questions",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4534,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "owned-location tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-grace-questions",
        "field": "labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      },
      {
        "row": 4793,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder owned-location italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-two-grace-questions",
        "field": "item.labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-augustine-study"
      },
      {
        "row": 4794,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder owned-location italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-two-grace-questions",
        "field": "item.labelByLocation",
        "context": "divinity-grace-alcove"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0940",
    "text": "Augustine asks how God helps a person want and do what is right. Luther asks what makes a person right with God. Both concern God's gift, but answering one question does not fully answer the other.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4535,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "two-grace-questions",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4791,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-two-grace-questions",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0941",
    "text": "Luther: bodily discipline trains me; it does not buy God\u2019s acceptance",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4536,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "practice-not-price",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4796,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-practice-not-price",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0942",
    "text": "For Luther, bodily work and discipline can train a person for service. Effort matters without becoming the price of God's acceptance.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4537,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "practice-not-price",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4795,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-practice-not-price",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0943",
    "text": "Zwingli: a ring recalls a beloved without containing their body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4538,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "remembered-ring",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0944",
    "text": "A ring can bring a loved person to mind without containing their body. Zwingli uses this example to explain how Communion's bread can point to Christ without containing his body.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4539,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "remembered-ring",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0945",
    "text": "Zwingli: Christ\u2019s human body is in heaven",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4540,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "body-in-heaven",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0946",
    "text": "Zwingli argues that Christ's human body is in heaven after the Ascension. He therefore reads the Communion bread as a sign of that body, not a place where the body is located.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4541,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "body-in-heaven",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0947",
    "text": "Luther: Christ\u2019s words give his body with the bread",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4542,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "luther-word-makes",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0948",
    "text": "In the 1529 catechism, the sacrament depends on Christ\u2019s words, not the participant\u2019s ability to create it by believing. This is not Aquinas\u2019s account of changed bread.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4543,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "luther-word-makes",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0949",
    "text": "Case: a Communion guest eats the bread without trusting Christ\u2019s promise",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4544,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "unbelieving-guest",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0950",
    "text": "The guest tests two questions: what is received, and whether receiving it brings the promised benefit. The two need not have the same answer in Luther\u2019s account.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4545,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "unbelieving-guest",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0951",
    "text": "Luther: Communion\u2019s promised forgiveness is received only through faith\u2014trust in Christ\u2019s promise",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4546,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "faith-benefit",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0952",
    "text": "For Luther, the promised forgiveness in Communion is received through faith: trusting Christ's promise that the gift is for you. Merely eating does not supply that trust. He distinguishes receiving Christ's body from receiving the forgiveness that also strengthens faith.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4547,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "faith-benefit",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0953",
    "text": "Marburg\u2019s signers affirm one God in three persons",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4548,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "signed-trinity",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0954",
    "text": "The jointly signed first article affirms the Trinity. Agreement on this matter does not remove their dispute about the supper.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4549,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "signed-trinity",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0955",
    "text": "Marburg: Christ is received through faith; his bodily presence stays disputed",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4550,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "signed-supper",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0956",
    "text": "The signers affirm receiving Christ through faith and the supper's strengthening of faith. They still disagree about Christ's bodily presence in bread and wine; they do not share one account of how that presence works.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4551,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "signed-supper",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0957",
    "text": "Zwingli: bread points to Christ\u2019s body; it does not contain it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4552,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "zwingli-reading",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0958",
    "text": "Zwingli's ring recalls someone without containing their body. Together with his belief that Christ's human body is in heaven, this supports his reading of Communion bread as a sign. Aquinas and Luther give different accounts of the same supper words.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4553,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "zwingli-reading",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0959",
    "text": "Aquinas: bread becomes Christ\u2019s body. Luther: Christ\u2019s body comes with bread",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4554,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "two-presence-accounts",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0960",
    "text": "Both affirm bodily presence, but the material accounts differ. Aquinas describes a change in what was bread; Luther\u2019s catechism calls it bread with Christ\u2019s body.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4555,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "two-presence-accounts",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0961",
    "text": "Aquinas: bread becomes the body. Luther: body with bread. Zwingli: bread signifies body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4556,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "three-supper-accounts",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4798,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-three-supper-accounts",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0962",
    "text": "Aquinas: the bread becomes Christ\u2019s body while appearances remain. Luther: Christ\u2019s body is given with the bread. Zwingli: the bread signifies the body, which is in heaven.\n\nThese are three different accounts of Communion. Shared words about Christ do not make their claims about bread and body identical.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4557,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "three-supper-accounts",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4797,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-three-supper-accounts",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0963",
    "text": "Luther: even an unbelieving Communion guest receives Christ\u2019s body with the bread",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4558,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "guest-not-maker",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0964",
    "text": "In Luther\u2019s account of Communion, even the guest who does not believe receives Christ\u2019s body with the bread. Christ\u2019s words establish what is given; the guest\u2019s disbelief does not undo it.\n\nThis answers what is received. Whether receiving it brings the promised forgiveness is a separate question.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4559,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "guest-not-maker",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0965",
    "text": "Luther: the unbelieving Communion guest receives Christ\u2019s body, not the promised forgiveness",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4560,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "received-not-benefited",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4800,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-received-not-benefited",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0966",
    "text": "Luther says an unbelieving Communion guest still receives Christ's body with the bread, because Christ's words establish the gift. Without trusting the promise, the guest does not receive its promised forgiveness. What is given and its benefit to the receiver are separate questions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4561,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "received-not-benefited",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4799,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-received-not-benefited",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0967",
    "text": "They agree about one God in three persons\u2014not every claim about Communion",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4562,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "shared-trinity",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0968",
    "text": "The writers can share belief in one God as Father, Son and Spirit while disagreeing about Communion. Real agreement does not require agreement on every question.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4563,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "shared-trinity",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0969",
    "text": "Shared belief in the Trinity leaves their Communion dispute open",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4564,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "bounded-agreement",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4802,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-bounded-agreement",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0970",
    "text": "At Marburg, the signers could affirm one God in three persons and receiving Christ through faith. They still disagreed about Christ\u2019s body being present in the bread and wine.\n\nA shared signature does not erase the disagreement. The 1529 articles record both the agreement and its limit.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4565,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "bounded-agreement",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0971",
    "text": "Council of Trent: God helps first, before an adult responds",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4566,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-first-help",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0972",
    "text": "Trent begins with God's help, which the person has not earned. Its account does not say that people start by saving themselves.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4567,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-first-help",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0973",
    "text": "Council of Trent: an adult can accept God\u2019s help or refuse it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4568,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-can-refuse",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0974",
    "text": "Trent says an adult can accept or refuse help that God gives first. The person's response is real, while the first gift remains unearned.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4569,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-can-refuse",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0975",
    "text": "Council of Trent: being made right with God for the first time is not earned by faith or deeds",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4570,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-no-price",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0976",
    "text": "The Council of Trent says that nothing before our first being made right with God\u2014neither faith nor deeds\u2014earns that gift. It begins with God\u2019s help.\n\nThis is initial justification. Keeping that limit visible prevents the false contrast \u201cLuther teaches a gift; Trent teaches buying it\u201d.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4571,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-no-price",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0977",
    "text": "Trent council: later deeds, helped by God, deepen received righteousness\u2014our renewed inner life with God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4572,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-growth",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0978",
    "text": "For Trent, righteousness includes God renewing the person within, not merely a change in reputation. After the initial gift, good deeds made possible by God\u2019s help increase this received righteousness.\n\nThis is the council\u2019s account of growth in justification. It is not just the observation that repeated practice can improve someone\u2019s outward behaviour, and it does not say people begin by earning salvation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4573,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-growth",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0979",
    "text": "Luther: deeds can train us, but do not make a Christian more holy before God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4574,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "luther-fruit",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0980",
    "text": "In Christian Liberty, Luther gives deeds a role in training the body and serving others, but denies that those deeds make an already-Christian person more holy before God.\n\nHis bishop comparison makes the distinction: doing the bishop\u2019s work does not make the bishop more consecrated. The text allows growth of faith and love, so this is not a denial of all growth or better conduct.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4575,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "luther-fruit",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0981",
    "text": "Trent: God helps us respond; we do not start by saving ourselves",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4576,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "assisted-response",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0982",
    "text": "In Trent's account, God's help comes first and a person really responds. Receiving help does not mean there is no human action.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4577,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "assisted-response",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0983",
    "text": "Trent: God helps first, but the adult really accepts or refuses",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4578,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "assisted-consent",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0984",
    "text": "Trent says the adult can accept or refuse God's prior help. Having a real choice does not mean the response earns the gift.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4579,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "assisted-consent",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0985",
    "text": "Trent council: an adult\u2019s response does not earn being made right with God for the first time",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4580,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "response-not-price",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4804,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-response-not-price",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0986",
    "text": "Trent describes an adult responding to God's help without earning the initial gift of being made right with God. This addresses initial justification, not every later role of good deeds.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4581,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "response-not-price",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4803,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-response-not-price",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0987",
    "text": "Luther and Trent: feeding someone does not earn our first acceptance by God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4582,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "gift-common-ground",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4806,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-gift-common-ground",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0988",
    "text": "In this household case, both accounts deny that feeding someone buys the initial gift of being made right with God. That limited agreement does not make their accounts of faith, inner renewal and later deeds identical.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4583,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "gift-common-ground",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0989",
    "text": "Trent and Luther dispute how deeds affect holiness before God\u2014not whether conduct can improve",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4584,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "works-dispute",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4808,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-works-dispute",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0990",
    "text": "Trent says deeds made possible by God's help increase the righteousness already received, including inward renewal. Luther's text denies that deeds make an already-Christian person more holy before God, while valuing training and service. The disagreement is about the role of deeds before God, not merely whether behaviour improves.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4585,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "works-dispute",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4807,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-works-dispute",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0991",
    "text": "Case: \u201cPlease pray for my child,\u201d to a living friend",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4586,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "friend-request",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0992",
    "text": "The request asks another person to pray to God. It does not ask the friend to replace God or to supply divine power.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4587,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "friend-request",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0993",
    "text": "Calvin allows living believers to pray for one another",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4588,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "calvin-mutual",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0994",
    "text": "Calvin allows Christians to ask a living neighbour to pray. He does not think this replaces Christ's unique role between people and God.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4589,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "calvin-mutual",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0995",
    "text": "Case: to a dead saint, \u201cStephen, pray for my child\u201d",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4590,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "saint-request",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0996",
    "text": "Someone asks a departed saint to pray to God on their behalf. They are asking for prayer, not a second saviour. Calvin and Trent disagree about whether people should make this request.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4591,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "saint-request",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0997",
    "text": "Calvin: asking dead saints for prayer lacks biblical permission and obscures Christ\u2019s unique role before God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4592,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "calvin-hearing",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0998",
    "text": "Calvin asks what biblical authority permits addressing saints who have died, and how they would know particular requests. He also thinks the practice draws attention away from Christ\u2019s unique work for us.\n\nThat work is called mediation: Christ\u2019s role between people and God. Saying that the saint is only a helper does not answer Calvin\u2019s objections.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4593,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "calvin-hearing",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0999",
    "text": "Case: a painting of Stephen, proposed for prayerful honour in a chapel",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4594,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "stephen-panel",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1000",
    "text": "The proposed chapel painting shows Stephen remaining faithful. The question is whether people should direct religious honour through it, not whether all paintings should be forbidden.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4595,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "stephen-panel",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1001",
    "text": "Calvin allows some pictures, but not honouring them in worship",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4596,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "calvin-pictures",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1002",
    "text": "Calvin is not simply against all art. His distinction concerns the use made of pictures in worship, including whether honour can safely be directed through them.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4597,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "calvin-pictures",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1003",
    "text": "Case: a bone labelled \u201cStephen\u201d; nobody has supplied its history",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4598,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "stephen-fragment",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1004",
    "text": "The bone is labelled Stephen, but there is no record of where it was found or who kept it. The label alone does not establish whose bone it is.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4599,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "stephen-fragment",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1005",
    "text": "A label records a claim; it does not prove identity",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4600,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "label-not-proof",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1006",
    "text": "A name on a label states whose bone someone claims this is. It does not prove the identity. Even a tradition that permits relics still needs evidence about this particular object.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4601,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "label-not-proof",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1007",
    "text": "Calvin: even a real saint\u2019s bone should not receive religious honour",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4602,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "calvin-even-genuine",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1008",
    "text": "Calvin objects both to doubtful relic claims and to giving relics religious honour. Establishing a bone's identity would not answer his objection to the practice.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4603,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "calvin-even-genuine",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1009",
    "text": "Calvin: asking a living friend to pray does not replace Christ",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4604,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "living-prayer",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4810,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-living-prayer",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1010",
    "text": "Calvin permits asking a living friend to pray while relying on Christ. This answers the living-friend case, not every proposed request for help.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4605,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "living-prayer",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4809,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-living-prayer",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1011",
    "text": "Calvin: asking dead saints for prayer lacks biblical permission and obscures Christ\u2019s unique work of speaking for us before God",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4606,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "saint-warrant-question",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1012",
    "text": "Calvin argues that Scripture does not authorize asking departed saints for prayer and that doing so obscures Christ's unique work for people before God. Calling the saint a helper does not answer these objections.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4607,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "saint-warrant-question",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1013",
    "text": "God can use helpers; Calvin still says asking dead saints for prayer lacks biblical permission and sidelines Christ",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4608,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "agency-not-permission",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4812,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-agency-not-permission",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1014",
    "text": "God\u2019s working through baptism shows a possible role for created means; water is not a person being asked for prayer. That example does not authorize addressing departed saints.\n\nCalvin affirms Christ\u2019s unique, continuing work of bringing people before God. He says asking departed saints lacks biblical permission and obscures that work. He is objecting to the practice, not doubting Christ\u2019s role.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4609,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "agency-not-permission",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4811,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-agency-not-permission",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1015",
    "text": "Calvin rejects honouring this painting in worship, not all paintings",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4610,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "calvin-panel-answer",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4814,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-calvin-panel-answer",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1016",
    "text": "Calvin rejects giving this painting a role in religious honour. His objection concerns its use in worship, not the existence of every painted picture.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4611,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "calvin-panel-answer",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4813,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-calvin-panel-answer",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1017",
    "text": "The name on the bone does not establish whose bone it is",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4612,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "fragment-unverified",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4816,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-fragment-unverified",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1018",
    "text": "The fragment's label is not enough to establish whose bone it is. The honest result is uncertainty, not an authenticated relic.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4613,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "fragment-unverified",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4815,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-fragment-unverified",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1019",
    "text": "Trent: saints with Christ pray for people on earth",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4614,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-saints-pray",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1020",
    "text": "Trent teaches that saints with Christ continue to pray for people on Earth. The council therefore recommends asking for their help.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4615,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-saints-pray",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1021",
    "text": "Trent: Christ alone saves; saints are not other saviours",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4616,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-christ-alone",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1022",
    "text": "The council does not present saints as competing saviours. It nevertheless disagrees with Calvin about the legitimacy of requesting their aid.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4617,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-christ-alone",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1023",
    "text": "Trent: honour the person shown in the picture, not the paint",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4618,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-image-honour",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1024",
    "text": "The council denies that divinity or power resides in an image as such. It gives images a role in remembrance, instruction and honour directed to their subjects.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4619,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-image-honour",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1025",
    "text": "Trent: saints\u2019 bodies deserve honour because they belong to Christ",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4620,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-body-honour",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1026",
    "text": "The decree treats holy bodies as connected with Christ and with resurrection. This is a reason within its teaching, not an automatic identification of any labelled fragment.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4621,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-body-honour",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1027",
    "text": "Trent: newly claimed relics need examination and a bishop\u2019s approval",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4622,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "trent-new-relic",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1028",
    "text": "The decree restricts recognition of new relics and approval of unusual images. A permissible category is not a licence for every particular object.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4623,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "trent-new-relic",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1029",
    "text": "Case update: a record of who has kept this bone",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4624,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "new-record",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1030",
    "text": "A new record identifies some of the people who kept the bone. It strengthens the investigation, but gaps in its history remain and a bishop has not recognized it as a relic.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4625,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "new-record",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1031",
    "text": "Trent: ask saints to pray through Christ, not to replace him",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4626,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "saints-not-saviours",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1032",
    "text": "Trent says saints with Christ pray for people on earth. Asking for their prayers therefore means asking for help through Christ, not replacing him. Calvin still rejects the practice because he finds no biblical permission for it and thinks it obscures Christ's unique role.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4627,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "saints-not-saviours",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1033",
    "text": "Trent: saints pray through Christ. Calvin: no biblical permission; Christ is sidelined",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4628,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4818,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1034",
    "text": "Trent says saints pray through Christ rather than replacing him. Calvin rejects asking them, arguing that it lacks biblical permission and obscures Christ's unique role. They disagree about whether people should make these requests, not simply about what to call the saints.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4629,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4817,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-prayer-disagreement",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1035",
    "text": "Trent allows honour directed through the painting to Stephen",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4630,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "panel-possible",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1036",
    "text": "Trent allows honour to pass through a painting to the person shown. The proposed Stephen painting fits that kind of use; the paint itself is not treated as divine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4631,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "panel-possible",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1037",
    "text": "Trent permits this honour through a picture; Calvin rejects it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4632,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4820,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1038",
    "text": "Trent says honour can pass through the picture to Stephen. Calvin rejects that devotional use. Both have now considered the same proposed painting.\n\nRedirecting the honour away from the paint explains Trent\u2019s position; it does not make Calvin accept it.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4633,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      },
      {
        "row": 4819,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-panel-still-disputed",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1039",
    "text": "Honouring saints\u2019 bones requires knowing this bone is a saint\u2019s",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4634,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "honour-needs-identity",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1040",
    "text": "A reason to honour genuine relics does not establish that this fragment is genuine. The object's identity still needs evidence.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4635,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "honour-needs-identity",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1041",
    "text": "This bone still needs examination and a bishop\u2019s recognition",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4636,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "recognition-pending",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1042",
    "text": "The claim about this bone still needs examination and a bishop's recognition. A name on its label and a partial history are not enough.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4637,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "recognition-pending",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1043",
    "text": "A record of the bone\u2019s past helps; it is not a bishop\u2019s approval",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4638,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "record-not-ruling",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1044",
    "text": "The new record helps trace who kept the bone. It does not verify every link in its history or amount to a bishop's approval.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4639,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
