        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "health-not-moral-test",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1051",
    "text": "Luther: the pope can lift church penalties, not control God\u2019s mercy",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4646,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "papal-penalty-limit",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1052",
    "text": "In 1517 Luther limits the pope's own power to penalties imposed by church authority. He distinguishes declaring God's forgiveness from controlling it. The limits he proposes are disputed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4647,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "papal-penalty-limit",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1053",
    "text": "Luther: an indulgence letter cannot command God to free a dead soul",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4648,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "letter-limited",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1054",
    "text": "An indulgence concerns penalties remaining after forgiveness. Luther further limits church authority: a papal letter cannot by its own power command God to release a dead soul.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4649,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "letter-limited",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1055",
    "text": "Luther: Christ\u2019s body comes with bread. Zwingli: bread points to the body",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4650,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "luther-zwingli-contrast",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1056",
    "text": "These two accounts differ about bodily presence. That does not yet locate Aquinas: his earlier changed-bread account is a third position to compare.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4651,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "luther-zwingli-contrast",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1057",
    "text": "Even if it is Stephen\u2019s bone, Calvin still rejects honouring it",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4652,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "authenticity-not-permission",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1058",
    "text": "The bone's identity remains unresolved, but Calvin's objection to honouring it does not depend on that uncertainty. A genuine object can still be disputed as a religious practice.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4653,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "authenticity-not-permission",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C1059",
    "text": "The record helps trace the bone; it does not yet prove its identity",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4654,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "record-adds-evidence",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
